From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <spolack+claude@mailbox.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:10:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] udht: allow building as a library

Rename main() to udht_main() and keep main() as a thin wrapper that is
compiled out with -DUDHT_LIBRARY. An embedder that cannot spawn processes
(an Android app) can then run the DHT node from its own entry point; the
argv interface stays as it is.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PVGaNeNhqp11rTLwZ9rM4J
---
 udht.c | 9 ++++++++-
 udht.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/udht.c b/udht.c
index cce4d40..9162364 100644
--- a/udht.c
+++ b/udht.c
@@ -654,7 +654,7 @@ int udht_reconnect(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
-int main(int argc, char **argv)
+int udht_main(int argc, char **argv)
 {
 	const char *progname = argv[0];
 	uint8_t auth_key[CURVE25519_KEY_SIZE];
@@ -715,3 +715,10 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv)
 
 	return 0;
 }
+
+#ifndef UDHT_LIBRARY
+int main(int argc, char **argv)
+{
+	return udht_main(argc, argv);
+}
+#endif
diff --git a/udht.h b/udht.h
index c85a1e6..529fdf3 100644
--- a/udht.h
+++ b/udht.h
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #ifndef __UDHT_H
 #define __UDHT_H
 
+int udht_main(int argc, char **argv);
 int udht_reconnect(void);
 void udht_network_add(const uint8_t *auth_key, int seq);
 void udht_network_flush(int seq);
